+### 5.2 Provenance of every shown salary
+Counts are from `stats.json` `provenance`; "×hour" means annualized ×2080 and "×month" ×12.
+
+| Board | Source counts |
+|---|---|
+| Amazon | structured 13,630: one row 8,425, hourly rows 2,583, one place of several 2,134, single figures 344, monthly 98, span of places 50, stated annual 3. Text 349 (the older national sentence "ranges from $X/year in our lowest geographic market up to $Y/year", read as Amazon states it, 20) |
+| Apple | text 2,390: one footer; 136 hourly. Structured 391: span of a requisition's footers, `salary.ranges` with places |
+| Google | text 2,512: one line 2,467 (incl. 3 yearly fixed-term), single figures 35, degree-line spans 7 |
+| Meta | structured 948: public_compensation; 45 monthly (interns) |
+| Microsoft | text 1,566: one range 1,344 (+30 hourly, 23 monthly, 4 yearly fixed-term), level spans 157, single figures 7, one other span 1 |
+| NVIDIA | text 1,462: level spans 887, one range 526 (+48 hourly interns), one five-range span 1 |
+| Netflix | text 259: one range per role (3 hourly) |
+
+- **Made by our code:** 0 estimates, 0 defaults, 0 level-band fills and 0 "±x% around a point". `job.salary`
+  is only ever `source: 'text'` or `'structured'`. Compstimate's estimate is a separate "about $X" line and
+  never fills `job.salary`.
+- **Conversions:** hourly ×2080 (Amazon 2,705, Apple 138, NVIDIA 48, Microsoft 44, Netflix 3), monthly ×12
+  (Amazon 174, Meta 45, Microsoft 30), and Austria's stated 14-payment annual figure (3). The currency is
+  never converted on the card; the chart converts to USD for placement only. The card rounds to thousands
+  ("$144K"); the drawer keeps the posted figures.
+- **Code paths that set or widen min/max or ranges[]:**
+  - `normalize.js#deriveSalary`, the structured currency pick: the span of one currency's
+    `raw.payRanges`, used when the structured currency is not the job's country's.
+  - `salary.js#parseSalary`:
+    - the national or city level group, at most 4×;
+    - one country's lines, at most 3× (Google degrees);
+    - an adjacent tier list, at most 3× (NVIDIA's five ranges);
+    - the "for Level N" tiers.
+  - `apple.js#spanPay` and `upgradeAppleJobs`: the span of a requisition's footers.
+  - `amazon.js#amazonSalary`: one row, never widened; the statedAnnual case sets min to the stated annual
+    figure.
+  - `toJobSalary`: annualizing, and min = max for a single figure.
+  - `vet.js` only quarantines; it never changes numbers.
+  - `upgrade.js#upgradeAmazonJobs`: rebuilds the table from stored `salary.ranges` (VT-22); the
+    reconstructed row text reads "68700 - 92700 USD year", not Amazon's wording.
