+| Levels (NVIDIA, Microsoft) | the span, unmarked (SA-1) | the span's bar and midpoint; the tip lists the levels | the span's midpoint |
+| Apple, a range per place | the span, "· N places" | the span's midpoint (SA-5 under a Location filter) | each place on its own range |
+| Amazon, a row per place | one place's row, called a span (SA-2) | that row's midpoint; the tip calls it a span (SA-2, SA-5) | each place on its own row (DQ-33 fixed) |
+| Google | the national band | its midpoint | its midpoint in every US city (the band covers every US location) |
+| Microsoft, SF/NYC | the national band, unless all US places are in those areas | the same | the same |
+
+- Several US pay zones are never collapsed into one min-of-mins to max-of-maxes range, except Apple's
+  footers (labelled, with each place's range kept) and the level spans.
+- Google, Meta and Microsoft publish one national band, not zones. Amazon's rows are kept per place.
